  "source_message": "feat(compliance): G-04 Trust Boundaries — OrchestrationTree + 34 tests (203/203 suite)

Implements GAP-REGISTER G-04: formal trust boundary enforcement between agents
in the BANXE multi-agent compliance stack.

── New: src/compliance/agents/orchestration_tree.py ─────────────────────────
AgentDescriptor (frozen dataclass):
  - agent_id, level (1/2/3), capabilities (tuple), trust_zone (GREEN/AMBER/RED)
  - has_capability() helper

TrustViolation dataclass:
  - caller_id, callee_id, rule (B-01..B-06), message, blocked (True=hard, False=warn)

TrustBoundaryError(RuntimeError):
  - Carries list[TrustViolation]; raised by assert_call_allowed() on any blocked violation

OrchestrationTree:
  - register() / get() / registered_ids()
  - check_call(caller, callee) → list[TrustViolation]  (all violations)
  - can_call(caller, callee)   → bool  (True only when no blocked violations)
  - assert_call_allowed()      → raises TrustBoundaryError or returns warnings
  - check_capability()         → TrustViolation | None  (B-06 policy_write guard)

Boundary rules:
  B-01  Level-2 → Level-1  BLOCKED  (lateral privilege escalation)
  B-02  Level-3 → Level-1  BLOCKED
  B-03  Level-3 → Level-2  BLOCKED  (adapters must call through Ports)
  B-04  RED → GREEN         BLOCKED  (untrusted → trusted boundary)
  B-05  AMBER → GREEN       WARN     (audited, not blocked)
  B-06  Level-2/3 + policy_write  BLOCKED  (I-22 PolicyPort read-only)

get_default_tree() singleton with all BANXE agents pre-registered:
  Level-1: banxe_aml_orchestrator
  Level-2: aml_orchestrator, tx_monitor, sanctions_check, crypto_aml
  Level-3: watchman_adapter(AMBER), jube_adapter(AMBER), yente_adapter(AMBER),
           clickhouse_writer(GREEN)

── Modified: src/compliance/banxe_aml_orchestrator.py ──────────────────────
Added Step 1 (trust boundary check) before _layer2_assess:
  - get_default_tree().assert_call_allowed("banxe_aml_orchestrator", "aml_orchestrator")
  - Any AMBER→GREEN warnings logged via _log.warning_event("TRUST_BOUNDARY_WARN")
  - TrustBoundaryError propagates as hard failure (blocked call aborts assess())

Tests: test_orchestration_tree.py T-01..T-34 — 34 passed
  T-01..T-02: AgentDescriptor immutability + has_capability
  T-03..T-08: Level-based boundary rules
  T-09..T-10: Zone-based rules (B-04 blocked, B-05 warn)
  T-11..T-12: Capability rules B-06 (Level-2 blocked, Level-1 allowed)
  T-13..T-16: assert_call_allowed + can_call
  T-17..T-18: Unknown agents default to Level-3 RED (conservative)
  T-19..T-21: check_capability policy_write enforcement
  T-22..T-29: Default tree — singleton + all agent levels + call matrix
  T-30..T-33: TrustBoundaryError + fresh instance isolation + re-register + ids
  T-34: Integration smoke-test — banxe_aml_orchestrator imports with tree active

Full suite: 203/203 passed

